 in Q3 2026 to 165bp.\n- Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so the stronger issuers can borrow.\n\n**Equity:**\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering because demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in Q3 2026.\n\n**Result:**\n- Norvane looks able to fund its plan through bonds, at wider spreads.\n- Pellham has not replaced the lost equity with debt. It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves. I can't tell why from the documents. It may be a leverage or rating limit, or a choice to protect its credit.\n- Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, so its cuts will hit suppliers.\n\n**Gaps:** The evidence is thin, drawn from three documents. I found no data on either company's leverage, rating headroom, total funding need or planned debt issuance. I also found nothing on equity valuations or other funding sources. So I can't size the overall shortfall beyond Pellham's withdrawn C$2.4B.","ttft_ms":1471,"type":"result","duration_ms":28216,"uuid":"f9e7e1cf-30fd-4589-afb8-91bd52bc4401","ttft_stream_ms":1247,"time_to_request_ms":178,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":16,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":34,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":16,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":5,"request_announcements":17,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":7,"message_normalization":6,"client_creation":9,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":46,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":78,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":199,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":126,"process_rss_mib_result":197,"process_anon_mib_result":116,"process_peak_rss_mib":199,"process_cpu_ms_turn":547,"pro